module laed-local-rules.local-rules

import core.states.louisiana.{ frcp6-louisiana }

// The Eastern District of Louisiana's own civil periods, computed under
// the federal rules (FRCP 6(a) governs "any local rule"). A contested
// motion is noticed for a submission date: the noticed date is the date
// the motion is deemed submitted, after which no further briefing is
// allowed without leave, and no oral argument is held unless requested
// under LR 78.1 or ordered (LR 7.2). The reply under LR 7.5 is due "no
// later than 4:00 p.m., two working days before the noticed submission
// date"; a working day is counted here as a court day (FRCP 6(a)(6) legal
// holidays and weekends skipped), and the 4:00 p.m. cutoff is the rule's,
// not computed. LR 7.8 allows one ex parte extension of time to plead of
// 21 days from the time the pleading would otherwise be due, on the
// movant's certification of no previous extension and no objection of
// record; it extends an FRCP period and declares none of its own, so it
// stays in this note. Rules that state no period or limit stay out:
// motion memoranda (7.4), consent motions (7.3, 7.6), the scheduling order
// (16.1), disclosure timing, which the court sets (26.1), review of a
// magistrate judge's order, noticed for submission as a motion (72.2), and
// attorney's fees, which need a verified contemporaneous report (54.2).
// The clerk's call of the docket on 14 days' notice for cases pending 90
// days without issue joined (16.2) and dismissal for failure to correct a
// returned address within 35 days (41.3.1) are court actions on the
// court's own motion, so they stay in this note. The earlier E.D. La.
// outline's FRCP flow and its decisions (Twombly, Iqbal, Celotex,
// Anderson, Matsushita, Frow v. De La Vega) are FRCP authority and belong
// to lit/frcp; they are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// A trial brief or memorandum supporting or opposing a motion: at most
/// 25 pages, excluding exhibits, except with prior leave of court
/// (E.D. La. LR 7.7).
limit memorandum { pages <= 25 cite "E.D. La. LR 7.7" } cite "E.D. La. LR 7.7"
/// A reply brief or memorandum: at most 10 pages, excluding exhibits,
/// except with prior leave of court (E.D. La. LR 7.7).
limit reply-memorandum { pages <= 10 cite "E.D. La. LR 7.7" } cite "E.D. La. LR 7.7"

/// A notice of removal is filed (E.D. La. LR 3.2).
event NoticeOfRemovalFiled()
/// A Motion to Consider Whether Another Party's Material Should Be Sealed
/// is filed and served on the Designating Party (E.D. La. LR 5.6(D)).
event OtherPartySealMotionFiled()
/// The court grants a motion to seal (E.D. La. LR 5.6(D)).
event SealMotionGranted()
/// The court denies a motion to file under seal (E.D. La. LR 5.6(G)).
event SealMotionDenied()
/// The noticed submission date of a contested motion (E.D. La. LR 7.2).
event SubmissionDate()
/// A motion is filed (E.D. La. LR 7.2).
event MotionFiled() paper memorandum
/// A memorandum in opposition to a motion is filed and served
/// (E.D. La. LR 7.5).
event OppositionFiled() paper memorandum
/// A reply brief in support of a motion is filed and served
/// (E.D. La. LR 7.5).
event ReplyFiled() paper reply-memorandum
/// A case is ordered separated from a consolidation (E.D. La. LR 10.2).
event DeconsolidationOrdered()
/// The scheduled preliminary conference (E.D. La. LR 26.2(A)).
event PreliminaryConference()
/// The scheduled FRCP 16(b) conference (E.D. La. LR 26.2(B)).
event SchedulingConference()
/// The prevailing party receives notice of entry of judgment
/// (E.D. La. LR 54.3).
event JudgmentEntryNoticed()
/// A party receives the opposition memorandum to a motion
/// (E.D. La. LR 78.1).
event OppositionReceived()
/// The case is finally disposed of (E.D. La. LR 79.3).
event FinalDisposition()
/// An order transferring a case to a district court outside the Fifth
/// Circuit is entered on the docket (E.D. La. LR 83.5.1).
event TransferOrderEntered()

/// E.D. La. LR 3.2: in every case in which a notice of removal is filed,
/// the moving defendant files, within 14 days of removal, a list of all
/// parties remaining in the action, copies of all pleadings filed in state
/// court, and copies of the returns of service filed in state court.
deadline removal-record-period: 14.days after NoticeOfRemovalFiled() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "E.D. La. LR 3.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// E.D. La. LR 5.6(D)(2)(b): within seven days of the filing of a Motion
/// to Consider Whether Another Party's Material Should Be Sealed, the
/// Designating Party files a statement or declaration supporting sealing;
/// failing to do so may result in unsealing without further notice.
deadline designating-party-statement-period: 7.days after OtherPartySealMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "E.D. La. LR 5.6(D)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// E.D. La. LR 5.6(D)(2)(c): any other party who wishes to respond to the
/// motion does so no later than 14 days after the motion is filed.
deadline other-party-seal-response-period: 14.days after OtherPartySealMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "E.D. La. LR 5.6(D)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// E.D. La. LR 5.6(D)(3): if the court grants the motion to seal, the
/// movant files a redacted version of the sealed document within 14 days
/// of the order granting the motion.
deadline redacted-version-period: 14.days after SealMotionGranted() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "E.D. La. LR 5.6(D)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// E.D. La. LR 5.6(G): if the motion to file under seal is denied, the
/// movant may file another motion to remove the documents from the record
/// within seven days; if none is timely filed, the documents are filed as
/// a public record.
deadline seal-denial-removal-period: 7.days after SealMotionDenied() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "E.D. La. LR 5.6(G)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// E.D. La. LR 7.2: unless otherwise ordered, actual notice of the
/// submission date is given to opposing counsel at least fifteen days
/// before the submission date, whatever FRCP 5(b) service method is used,
/// and the motion is filed not later than the fifteenth day preceding it.
deadline motion-notice-period: 15.days before SubmissionDate() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "E.D. La. LR 7.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// E.D. La. LR 7.5: each party opposing a motion files and serves a
/// memorandum in opposition no later than eight days before the noticed
/// submission date.
deadline opposition-period: 8.days before SubmissionDate() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "E.D. La. LR 7.5"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// E.D. La. LR 7.5: the movant may file and serve a reply brief no later
/// than 4:00 p.m., two working days before the noticed submission date.
deadline reply-period: 2.court_days before SubmissionDate() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "E.D. La. LR 7.5"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// E.D. La. LR 10.2: if a case is ordered separated from a consolidation,
/// counsel jointly designate the documents in the master record needed for
/// the separated case and file the designation within seven days of the
/// deconsolidation order.
deadline deconsolidation-designation-period: 7.days after DeconsolidationOrdered() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "E.D. La. LR 10.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// E.D. La. LR 26.2(A): except as otherwise ordered, the FRCP 26(f)
/// conference is held no later than seven working days before the
/// scheduled preliminary conference.
deadline rule26f-conference-period: 7.court_days before PreliminaryConference() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "E.D. La. LR 26.2(A)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// E.D. La. LR 26.2(B): when a party objects at the FRCP 26(f) conference
/// that initial disclosures are not appropriate, the parties file a
/// written discovery plan, including the nature of the objection, no later
/// than three working days before the scheduled Rule 16(b) conference.
deadline discovery-plan-report-period: 3.court_days before SchedulingConference() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "E.D. La. LR 26.2(B)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// E.D. La. LR 54.3: within 35 days of receiving notice of entry of
/// judgment, unless otherwise ordered, the party allowed costs serves and
/// files a motion to tax costs with a certification that the items are
/// correct and necessarily incurred.
deadline costs-motion-period: 35.days after JudgmentEntryNoticed() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "E.D. La. LR 54.3"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// E.D. La. LR 78.1: a party seeking oral argument files a separate
/// written request with the motion or opposition, or within three days
/// after receipt of the opposition memorandum; argument is held only if
/// ordered.
deadline oral-argument-request-period: 3.days after OppositionReceived() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "E.D. La. LR 78.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// E.D. La. LR 79.3: exhibits in the clerk's custody are removed within
/// 35 days of the final disposition of the case, or may be destroyed or
/// otherwise disposed of by the clerk.
deadline exhibit-removal-period: 35.days after FinalDisposition() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "E.D. La. LR 79.3"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// E.D. La. LR 83.5.1: unless all affected parties consent, an order
/// transferring a case to a district court outside the Fifth Circuit
/// (other than a JPML transfer order) is stayed for 21 days from its entry
/// on the docket.
deadline transfer-stay-period: 21.days after TransferOrderEntered() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "E.D. La. LR 83.5.1"
{
  forum frcp
}
